<p>Palestinian officials said local elections held on Saturday in the occupied West Bank and in Deir al-Balah in central Gaza were a success, framing the vote as an encouraging first step toward long-delayed presidential elections. The results showed candidates aligned with President Mahmoud Abbas and his Fatah movement winning most races, including seats in Gaza, while turnout differed sharply between the two territories: about 56% in the West Bank and 23% in Deir al-Balah. The Gaza vote carried extra symbolic weight because it was the first election of any kind there since 2006 and came after years of division between the Palestinian Authority in the West Bank and Hamas in Gaza. Palestinian Prime Minister Mohammad Mustafa said including Deir al-Balah was meant to show Gaza remained part of a future Palestinian state, even as the vote took place under difficult wartime conditions and after the Palestinian Authority had gone 21 years without a presidential election.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/FORixuSdX2sFSXgOyk6N0ToSVMpbC_3hxs9yGJdM1wRKcCl8x57tKQc-IxOgvqCE8lFcKhUIzTSTeyoPGBHnL7vYaKZzSuiEk8wXG97M3baA' alt='A Palestinian woman casts her ballot at a polling station during municipal elections in the village of al-Badhan, north of Nablus, in the Israeli-occupied West Bank on April 25, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Seat breakdown: In Deir al-Balah, Abbas loyalists won six of 15 municipal seats, while candidates widely seen as aligned with Hamas won two, according to preliminary results reported after the vote.</li><li>Hamas boycott: Hamas did not formally nominate candidates in Gaza and boycotted the election in the Israeli-occupied West Bank, a choice that helped set up a strong Fatah showing there.</li><li>Uncontested races: In many West Bank municipal contests, Fatah-aligned candidates won seats uncontested, helping the movement dominate the overall result.</li><li>Statehood message: Palestinian officials said holding the ballot in both territories was meant to reinforce that Gaza and the West Bank are part of one future state despite years of political separation.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Palestinian Authority: The Palestinian Authority described the vote as a successful democratic exercise and a bridge to future presidential elections and eventual statehood. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/palestinian-authorities-call-local-elections-in-a-central-gaza-community-and-the-occupied-west-bank-a-success'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Mohammad Mustafa: The Palestinian prime minister said the elections took place at a highly sensitive moment under complex and exceptional circumstances, but still marked the start of a broader national democratic process. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995318/pa-loyalists-win-big-in-palestinian-municipal-polls'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Hamas: Hamas stayed out of the formal race in Gaza and boycotted voting in the West Bank, underscoring the continuing split with the Palestinian Authority even as some Gaza candidates were seen locally as close to the movement. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995318/pa-loyalists-win-big-in-palestinian-municipal-polls'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera: Low turnout in Gaza reflected the continuing effects of the war there, even as Abbas loyalists swept many seats. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/26/abbas-loyalists-sweep-palestine-elections-in-occupied-west-bank-gaza-city'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/palestinian-authorities-call-local-elections-gaza-community-west-132403466'>Palestinian authorities call local elections in a Gaza community and the West Bank a success</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/26/abbas-loyalists-sweep-palestine-elections-in-occupied-west-bank-gaza-city'>Abbas loyalists sweep Palestinian elections, including some seats in Gaza</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/27/g-s1-118847/local-elections-in-gaza-and-the-west-bank'>Palestinian officials hail local elections in a Gaza community and the West Bank</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/palestinian-authorities-call-local-elections-in-a-central-gaza-community-and-the-occupied-west-bank-a-success'>Palestinian authorities call local elections in a central Gaza community and the occupied West Bank a success</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995318/pa-loyalists-win-big-in-palestinian-municipal-polls'>PA loyalists win big in Palestinian municipal polls</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>